(d) habitually commits or attempts to commit, or aids or abets the commission of any offence relating to property; Security for good behaviour for habitual offenders.
(e) habitually commits or attempts to commit, or aids or abets in the commission of, offence involving a breach of the peace; or (f) is so desperate or dangerous as to render his being at large without security hazardous to the community, such Magistrate may, in the manner provided in this Act, require such suspect to show cause why he should not be ordered to enter into a recognizance with sureties for his good behaviour for such period, not exceeding 3 years, as the Magistrate deems fit.

